.md
# Making slides
Type `.slide` in the first line of an input cell and start writing Markdown slide on a new line:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
# Making slides
Type `.slide` in the first line of an input cell and start writing Markdown slide on a new line:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide
# Presentation Title

You can also create presentations using the WLJS Notebook.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: slide
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
<dummy ># Presentation Title

You can also create presentations using the WLJS Notebook.</dummy>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md

Slide cells provide all features of Markdown cells, WLX cells and HTML, event listeners for slide events, fragment animations, and the option to export all slides as PDF.

:::info
To enter fullscreen mode, press the <kbd>f</kbd> key after focusing (click) on a slide.
:::

:::info
To enable virtual pointer, press the <kbd>q</kbd> key after focusing (click) on a slide.
:::

:::warning
Use the __project feature__ <kbd>Ctrl-Shift-Enter</kbd> or <kbd>⌘-Shift-Enter</kbd> of cell properties to show slides in a separate window. Note that the slide cell will also be evaluated within the context of a new window
:::

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%

Slide cells provide all features of Markdown cells, WLX cells and HTML, event listeners for slide events, fragment animations, and the option to export all slides as PDF.

:::info
To enter fullscreen mode, press the <kbd >f</kbd> key after focusing (click) on a slide.
:::

:::info
To enable virtual pointer, press the <kbd >q</kbd> key after focusing (click) on a slide.
:::

:::warning
Use the __project feature__ <kbd >Ctrl-Shift-Enter</kbd> or <kbd >⌘-Shift-Enter</kbd> of cell properties to show slides in a separate window. Note that the slide cell will also be evaluated within the context of a new window
:::

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Basics
### Creating Individual Slides

Each `.slide` cell creates a single presentation slide. You can write multiple slides across different cells in your notebook:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Basics
### Creating Individual Slides

Each `.slide` cell creates a single presentation slide. You can write multiple slides across different cells in your notebook:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide
# First Slide
Content for the first slide

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide
# Second Slide
Content for the second slide

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
### Separating Slides Within a Cell
Within a single `.slide` cell, you can create multiple slides by separating them with 3 dashes:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
### Separating Slides Within a Cell
Within a single `.slide` cell, you can create multiple slides by separating them with 3 dashes:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide
# First Slide
This is the first slide

---

# Second Slide
This is the second slide

---

# Third Slide
This is the third slide

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
### Merging All Slides
To combine all slides from different cells across your notebook into a single presentation, use the plural form:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
### Merging All Slides
To combine all slides from different cells across your notebook into a single presentation, use the plural form:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slides

Thank you for the attention

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
This will merge and render all slide cells in the notebook as one continuous presentation, allowing you to navigate through all slides sequentially.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
This will merge and render all slide cells in the notebook as one continuous presentation, allowing you to navigate through all slides sequentially.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
