## Rows
Use plain HTML and plain CSS (or our predefined classes) to create rows and columns:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Rows
Use plain HTML and plain CSS (or our predefined classes) to create rows and columns:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide

# Example

<div class="flex justify-between">
<div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 1

Content goes...

Content goes... Content goes...

</div>
<div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 2

Content goes...

</div>
</div>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: slide
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
<dummy >
# Example

<div class="flex justify-between"><div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 1

Content goes...

Content goes... Content goes...

</div><div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 2

Content goes...

</div></div></dummy>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Alternatively you can use `Row` from the standard library of WL here too:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Alternatively you can use `Row` from the standard library of WL here too:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.slide

# Example

<Row Alignment={{{Left, Right}, Center}} ImageSize={{Full, Automatic}}>

<div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 1

Content goes...

Content goes... Content goes...

</div>
<div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 2

Content goes...

</div>
</Row>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: slide
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
<dummy >
# Example

<div class="flex flex-row" style="align-items:center;width:100%;"><div style="flex:1;display:flex;justify-content:flex-start;"><div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 1

Content goes...

Content goes... Content goes...

</div></div>
<div style="flex:1;display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;"><div class="text-left">

## Subtitle 2

Content goes...

</div></div></div></dummy>

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%


